  I have completed a thorough check of the Claim Approval and Notification System.

1. Admin Approve / Reject Functionality
I have verified that the Approve/Reject system is fully implemented:

Admin Console: When an administrator logs in and navigates to "Review Claims", they will see two clear buttons: Approve (Green) and Reject (Red).
Rejection Logic: If an admin clicks Reject, the system prompts for a Rejection Reason to ensure the employee is properly informed.
State Management: Once an action is taken, the claim's status is updated in the database, and the action buttons are hidden to prevent duplicate processing.
2. Enhanced Notification System (The "Notification Dialog")
To address your concern about missing notifications, I have implemented a multi-layered notification system that acts like a "dialog" at the top of the screen:

Dashboard Alerts: Both Admins and Employees now see a prominent alert section at the very top of their dashboard whenever there are unread messages.
Admins are instantly notified when a new claim is filed.
Employees are instantly notified when their claim is Approved or Rejected (including the reason).
Navbar Bell Indicator: I have added a Notification Bell to the navigation bar of every page. It displays a red badge with the count of unread notifications (e.g., "3"), so you know you have messages even if you aren't on the dashboard.
One-Click Dismiss: Users can click "Mark as Read" or "Dismiss" directly from their dashboard to clear the notification.
3. Automatic Triggers
Admin Side: Every time an employee clicks "Submit Claim", a notification is automatically generated for all "ROLE_ADMIN" users.
Employee Side: Every time an admin processes a claim, a personal notification is sent to that specific employee's dashboard.
